@startuml
title Two routes from a Poly-IOP to a SNARK
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor #F3EEFB
  BorderColor #7A5BB5
}
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #F3EEFB
  BorderColor #7A5BB5
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #7A5BB5
}
skinparam ArrowColor #7A5BB5

rectangle "Poly-IOP\n(prover sends bounded-degree polynomials,\nverifier evaluates them at points of F)" as PIOP

rectangle "Interactive proof" as IP1
rectangle "SNARK" as S1

rectangle "IOP\n(prover sends strings,\nverifier opens cells)" as IOP
rectangle "SNARK" as S2

PIOP -right-> IP1 : polynomial commitment scheme\n(polynomials -> commitments,\nqueries -> evaluation proofs)
IP1 -right-> S1 : Fiat-Shamir

PIOP -down-> IOP : Reed-Solomon IOPP\n(polynomial -> RS codeword,\nevaluation -> quotient proximity test)
IOP -right-> S2 : BCS compiler\n(Merkle commitments + Fiat-Shamir)

note bottom of IOP
  FRI is one efficient Reed-Solomon IOPP.
  It is applied to the quotient words that
  certify the requested evaluations.
end note
@enduml
